ep 5, before the manifest is read. I checked the wiring myself rather than trusting the notes:\n\n- `recheck` (`commit.go:420`) runs **after** `Journal.Recover` and **before** both `publishWinners` and `stageTargets` — the ordering the verdict demanded.\n- A generation mismatch maps to `restartClosure` (`commit.go:302`).\n- The closure-input audit holds: `LoadHybridDecls`/`HybridManifestPath` have exactly **one** install-path caller; the other two (`main.go:1000,1010`) are read-only `hybrid list`/`status`; `global.go` reads no hybrid manifest and locks `GlobalRoot(home)` at line 46 before any read.\n\nThe **digest-then-read** ordering is the good call here — a racing writer leaves a digest that no longer matches, so you restart. The reverse would record the writer's bytes while the closure came from the bytes you read, and commit stale activation invisibly.\n\n## Two things I caught that changed the work\n\n**The cycle-2 full-suite log was stale.** It finished at 17:02:45; `commit.go` was last modified at **17:15:33**. The directive said not to redo the full suite, but inheriting a log that predates the final edit by 13 minutes would have been a false claim. I re-ran the whole thing in three recorded chunks instead.\n\n**`setsid` doesn't exist on macOS.** My first detached runner produced literally nothing — silent failure. And a single-shell `go test ./...` got killed at exit 144, same as the prior run. Fix that stuck: bounded foreground commands plus a durable `<name>.exit` file written as the runner's last action, so a missing `.exit` reads as \"killed\", never \"passed\".\n\n## Gates — every one a standalone process, real exit codes\n\n| Gate | Exit |\n|---|---|\n| gofmt / `git diff --check` | 0, 0 |\n| `go build ./...` / `go vet ./...` | 0, 0 |\n| tests, all 40 packages (3 chunks) | 0 — atomicity 411.3s, install 236.0s, other 38 ok |\n| race — 4 new activation cases | 0 (427.0s) |\n| race — restart/concurrency/recovery | 0 (56.3s) |\n| race — staging + transaction | 0 |\n| `golangci-lint` v2.4.0 `run ./...` | **0 — `0 issues`** |\n\nNot claimed, and marked as such in the archive: the exit-144 shell, cycle-2's empty `gate-test-race.log`, and the stale full-suite log.\n\n## Worth the reviewer's attention\n\n`internal/install/atomicity` is at **411.3s plain against a 600s default timeout** — and 427.0s for the four activation cases *alone* under `-race`. CI runners are slower. The next case added there needs a split decision, not another four installs.\n\nWorktree `.temp/TASK-260720-1zntv0/worktree` is untouched — nothing staged, HEAD still `17804ce`. Attached: `TASK-260720-2284br_implementation-notes-rework-2.md` and `..._gate-evidence-rework-2.tar.gz`, plus a logbook entry.","ttft_ms":2255,"ttft_stream_ms":1751,"time_to_request_ms":63,"type":"result","duration_ms":1802717,"uuid":"67157c46-6a41-4e20-a8f1-672bec31afaf"}
